@page "/"
@namespace Theatre_TimeLine.Pages
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@{
    Layout = "_Layout";
}

@*
   We intentionally use Server render mode instead of ServerPrerendered here.
   When using ServerPrerendered, MudBlazor root providers such as MudThemeProvider
   and other JS-interop–driven services (dialogs, snackbars, popovers) are created
   during the prerendering pass before the authenticated user and circuit are fully
   established. On reconnect, these providers are reinitialized with a different
   authentication state, which has caused inconsistent theming, duplicate provider
   instances, and occasional JS interop errors.
   We tested ServerPrerendered and confirmed these issues only occur during the
   prerender phase with MudBlazor's providers. Alternatives such as deferring
   MudBlazor provider initialization, moving them out of the prerendered tree, or
   splitting the app into a prerendered shell plus an interactive MudBlazor region
   were evaluated but would have required larger structural changes.
   To prioritize stability over the initial perceived load-time benefit, we keep the
   App component in pure Server mode here. If the MudBlazor provider behavior during
   prerendering is improved in the future, this can be revisited.
*@
<component type="typeof(App)" render-mode="Server" />
